  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n   - We'll implement a multi-level optimization strategy using randomized local search and Gaussian process regression to explore promising regions of the solution space\n   - The algorithm will focus on active regions identified by gradients and repair self-overlaps using periodic adjustments and spectral constraints\n   - This approach avoids local optima by combining local search with multiple resolution levels and random exploration\n   - Key innovations include a repair mechanism that preserves integral constraints and spectral properties\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   - Optimized function: h(x) \u2208 [0,1] with 1/2 integral over [0,2]\n   - Objective to minimize: C5 = max_k \u222b h(x) [1-h(x+k)] dx\n   - Objective is approximated by finite difference matrix on grid points\n   - Constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, \u2211h[i] = n/2\n   - Repair mechanism ensures boundary conditions and integral constraint\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   - Initialize population with given parent solution (n0=280)\n   - Use adaptive repair function that maintains integral constraint\n   - For each generation:\n        * Generate candidate solutions by perturbing values in \"active regions\"\n        * Calculate fitness via correlation and repair invalid candidates\n        * Use Gaussian process regression to extrapolate and guide search\n        * Apply principal component analysis to identify periodic patterns\n   - Implement octree-based active region tracking\n   - Error-checking ensures valid solutions\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations:\n   - Parent template generation\n   - Two-level resource allocation (gradient-based for high resolution, stochastic for low resolution)\n   - Adaptive spectral weighting in repair function\n   - Progressive error reduction in correlation calculation\n\n5. Computational budget and robustness:\n   - Allocate resources dynamically based on gradient density\n   - Time monitoring ensures efficient execution (progress every 10 seconds)\n   - Budget: 1100 seconds, resolution doubling planned\n\n6. Validation and request contract:\n   - Repair function ensures 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 and exact integral\n   - Correlation calculated with boundary clipping\n   - Error propagation curve computed from stochastic perturbations\n   - Solution returned as (h_values, c5_bound, n_points)",
